AVOIDANCE OF CONTACT.

The majority of connections by marriage who are of
opposite sexes and between whom there is name avoidance
also avoid coming into contact with each other.

A man would most rigidly avoid talking to a sister of his
wife whether he met her alone or in the company of others.
If he met her alone he would avoid coming near her at all;
if this were impossible, as when meeting on a jungle track,
brother-in-law and sister-in-law would turn their backs to
each other in passing and one, usually the woman, would step
aside into the bushl

A man avoids his mother-in-law less rigidly than his wife's
sisters, although if he meets her alone he treats her in the
same way, and even in public does not usually enter her

